THIRD-PARTY DATA

This repository commits three tables derived from third-party sources rather than the
databases themselves: Test_sequences.csv and metabolite_binding_sequences_human.csv
are derived from UniProt (CC BY 4.0) and InterPro (CC0), and
Test_set_metabolite_SIMLES.xlsx carries ChEMBL identifiers (CC BY-SA 3.0). Attribution
for these sources is given in README.md, under "About the data".

A per-source survey of licences, provenance and redistribution verdicts
(docs/06-DATA-SOURCES.md) lives on the scaffold/initial-documentation branch. Sources
fetched at runtime carry their own terms. Users are responsible for complying with the
license of each data source they fetch.

SCIENTIFIC DISCLAIMER

Nothing produced by this software has been experimentally validated. Its outputs are
prioritised, falsified hypotheses with stated confidence, intended to inform experimental
planning. They are not evidence of a protein-ligand interaction, and they must not be used
as a basis for any clinical or diagnostic decision.
